## Parallelism cheat sheet

| Stage | Max parallel agents | Critical path |
|---|---|---|
| S0 | 3–4 | App boot → sample in workspace |
| S1 | 2–3 | Overlay coords → stroke feel |
| S2 | 2–3 | Facts → instruct submit |
| S3 | 3–4 | Stub fixture → apply → undo |
| S4 | 2–3 | Motion + brand + dry-run |
| S5 | 1–2 | Ports + reducer |

## Subagent prompt template

```text
You are implementing <SUBTASK_ID> — <title> for Monet.
Read docs/PRD.md, docs/TRD.md, and .cursor/rules/stages.mdc for context.
Own ONLY these paths: <owns>.
Do not expand scope into other subtasks.
Match existing stack: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, CSS Modules, Zustand, Zod.
Stub AI by default; no auth/multiplayer UI.
Done when: <deliverable from table>.
If blocked by a missing contract, stop and report the dependency.
When finished, respond with a full completion update: what is done (subtask + deliverable),
any remaining gaps, and concrete how-to-test steps (routes, commands, expected behavior, gate check).
```

## MVP acceptance checklist

- [ ] Rect + freehand lassos over sample page
- [ ] Scout shows ≥3 facts for a selection
- [ ] Instruction runs pipeline (stub OK) with Brief + Plan + Suggestion + Proof
- [ ] Stage rail reflects progress (or instant stub complete)
- [ ] ≥1 apply after Proof ok + undo
- [ ] Keyboard-usable primary chrome
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected
- [ ] `AuthPort` + `RealtimePort` + turn reducer present
- [ ] No AI secrets in client bundle
- [ ] Demo path works offline in stub mode
- [ ] No pin/lens/critique primary UX

## Out of scope (S0–S5)

Auth UI, Supabase, websockets, microservices, Figma plugin, headless browser farm, parallel specialist Craft agents (post-F2 only).
